Mobile title panel has max-height + overflow-y auto but animation sheetIn overrides translateX(-50%) (ends translate(-50%,0)), so horizontal centering survives but that's okay. It also overrides nothing vertical since top auto/bottom.

Desktop title panel needs centering. Simplest: remove transform: translateY(-50%) and set `top: max(20px, calc(50% - 293px))`? Not responsive. Better: `translate: 0 -50%;` and set transform none initially; keyframes panelIn transform won't override translate. Then mobile `transform: translateX(-50%)` still overwritten by panelIn end transform (translateY(0) scale(1)) => loses horizontal centering! Wait currently mobile title panel has animation sheetIn, which includes translate(-50%) so centered. If we switch to translate property only on desktop, mobile uses sheetIn, which includes -50%. That's consistent.

But when viewport width <860, `.title-panel` uses sheetIn so no problem. Desktop >860 uses panelIn. So fix desktop only:
```
.title-panel { top: 50%; translate: 0 -50%; }  /* remove transform: translateY(-50%) */
```
At width 861-1080 uses same. At max-height landscape (<=520) media sets `top:50%; transform: translate(-50%,-50%)`, but that media is within width possibly >860? For landscape phones width > height, could be 900x500. Then desktop panelIn + transform translate(-50%,-50%) overwritten by panelIn => vertically not centered (top 250, height max 480 => overflow). Need fix landscape rule too: set `translate: -50% -50%; transform: none;` and keep animation? panelIn's transform will compose with translate. Good.

Also title panel desktop height 586 at 793 fits. At 600-793 heights >586 fine. Could add `max-height: calc(100dvh - 24px); overflow-y:auto` for desktop too; but overflow-y auto would show scrollbar (can hide) and content could be cut. Better scale spacing via max-height media query.

Let's implement:
- `.title-panel`: remove transform, add `translate: 0 -50%; max-height: calc(100dvh - 20px); overflow-y: auto; scrollbar-width:none;` but overflow is currently hidden for decorative after; setting auto would allow scroll and still clip decorations. It also would allow Play access in smaller heights. Add hidden scrollbar rules globally.
- At mobile, existing max-height and overflow-y auto already; set translate: none? It uses `left:50%; transform: translateX(-50%)` but animation sheetIn includes transform so no initial? The final animation is translate(-50%,0), so it works while animation is active with fill mode both (always). Actually after animation ends with fill both, transform remains translate(-50%,0). So horizontal centering works. The `top:auto; bottom:...` positioning isn't affected. So fine. But our new base `translate: 0 -50%` would also apply to mobile and shift it up 50% of its own height! That would break mobile. Need override `translate: none` in mobile rule. Or avoid translate property and create a specific animation.

Maybe cleaner: define new keyframes for desktop title panel:
```
@keyframes titleRise {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(calc(-50% + 18px)) scale(.985); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1); }
}
.title-panel { transform: translateY(-50%); animation: titleRise .85s ... both; }
```
And media landscape:
```
@keyframes titleRiseLandscape { from { opacity:0; transform: translate(-50%, calc(-50% + 18px)) scale(.985);} to {opacity:1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1);} }
.title-panel { animation: titleRiseLandscape ... }
```
But mobile <=860 uses sheetIn which already handles translate(-50%,0) with bottom positioning. This is explicit and avoids `translate`. CSS keyframes near panelIn. Do that.

Also set `max-height: calc(100dvh - 24px); overflow-y:auto; scrollbar-width:none;` on base .title-panel to handle short desktop; add webkit scrollbar hide globally. This conflicts with decorative ::after which stays inset. Fine.

